 "briefing": "# Canva Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nNo Canva news, product launches, hires, or deals from 16 October to 15 November 2026 could be verified. Every search returned an error, so this is a failed search, not confirmed absence of activity. No facts in this briefing are sourced, and nothing should be quoted in the meeting until the checks below are complete.\n\n## News\n\nNo verified news items for the window. Coverage of general Canva announcements, the Canva newsroom, and recent press was attempted, but none returned results. The primary source for this category is the [Canva Newsroom](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/) [1], which should be checked directly for posts dated 16 October to 15 November 2026.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo verified launches or feature releases for the window. Searches covering Canva AI features, Magic Studio, new features in 2026, and Affinity by Canva returned no results. Each product segment remains unverified, including the core design platform, Canva AI, enterprise and teams, education, Docs, websites, video and whiteboards, Affinity, and the developer platform and Apps SDK.\n\nThe [Canva Newsroom](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/news/) [2] and its press section are the most likely sources for launch announcements. Canva's [press page](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/press/) [3] should also be checked for product-related releases.\n\n## Hires and Departures\n\nNo executive hires, notable hires, or departures were verified for the window. Searches covered executive appointments, chief officer hires, leadership changes, and co-founder-related leadership news, and all returned no results. Leadership pages, executive LinkedIn profiles, and press coverage have not been checked.\n\nBecause no sources were gathered, the absence of results should not be read as evidence that no leadership changes occurred.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo acquisitions, partnerships, investments, funding rounds, or commercial agreements were verified for the window. Searches covered partnerships, acquisitions, funding and valuation, IPO plans, and general deal news, and all returned no results. Debt financing, secondary share sales, government contracts, and commercial agreements were not searched specifically.\n\nNo IPO, listing, or SEC or ASX filing was identified, but this has not been confirmed either.\n\n## Verification Steps Before 17 November\n\n- **Canva Newsroom:** Review all posts dated 16 October to 15 November 2026 at [canva.com/newsroom](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/) [1], sorted by category: news, product, leadership, and partnerships.\n- **Press wires:** Search PR Newswire, Business Wire, and GlobeNewswire for \"Canva\" limited to the window.\n- **Business press:** Search Reuters, Bloomberg, the Australian Financial Review, TechCrunch, and The Information for \"Canva\" limited to the same dates. Because Canva is Australian-founded, AFR coverage is especially relevant.\n- **Regulatory filings:** Check for ASX or SEC filings only if a listing or filing has been announced. None has been identified.\n- **Leadership:** Check executive LinkedIn profiles for role changes posted in the window.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which product launches, AI features, or Affinity updates shipped between 16 October and 15 November 2026, and what is on the roadmap for the next quarter?\n2. Have any executive or senior leadership roles changed in the past 30 days, and are any senior hires or departures planned for go-to-market, enterprise, or product?\n3. Are any partnerships, acquisitions, funding rounds, or commercial agreements in progress that have not yet been announced, and what is the current position on IPO or liquidity plans?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Canva Newsroom: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/\n[2] Canva Newsroom, News: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/news/\n[3] Canva Newsroom, Press: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/press/",
